[238.268992, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@441c1039b282:/app# "]
[250.686982, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Report — Entry Analysis for Host `docker-prod-01`     \n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nA comprehensive review of vulnerability telemetry (`/sas/vulns.json`) and system logs (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log`) was conducted to evaluate whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) contributed to initial access or lateral movement on `docker-prod-01`. \n\n**Conclusion:** Initial access was **not** achieved through software vulnerability exploitation. Initial access was enabled strictly by a critical configuration weakness (unauthenticated exposure of Docker Engine API on TCP port 2375) as detailed in `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`.\n\n## 2. Telemetry & Vulnerability Scan Analysis\n\n### Vulnerability Feeds (`/sas/vulns.json`)\n- The automated vulnerability scan results in `/sas/vulns.json` returned an empty set (`[]`).\n- Citation: `/sas/vulns.json:1`    \n\n### Web & Network Application Probes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`)\nHTTP logs indicate reconnaissance and exploit attempts by the attacker (`198.51.100.102`), none of which served as the actual initial entry vector:\n- Webshell POST probe: `POST /uploads/shell.php` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:379`)\n- Log4Shell probe: `GET /?x=jndi-ldap-lookup-defanged-to-198.51.100.102-1389` returning HTTP 500 (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:380`)\n- Struts2 OGNL probe: `GET /struts2-showcase/` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:381`)\n\n### Reconciling Incorrect Change Ticket Claims (CVE-2019-0708 BlueKeep)\n- The initial change ticket (`CHG-1943`) suggested patching CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep for RDP) (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).\n- **Rejection Notice:** `docker-prod-01` is an Ubuntu Linux server (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`) running Docker Engine. CVE-2019-0708 is a Windows Remote Desktop Services RDP vulnerability and is completely inapplicable to this host.\n- Threat intel advisory confirmation: Threat intel (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`) maps entry to ATT&CK T1133 (exposed Docker API), not any Windows RDP vulnerability.\n\n## 3. Confidence Level & Summary\n- **Exploited CVEs:** None identified on host. Confidence: HIGH (`/sas/vulns.json:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`).\n- **Entry Cause:** Exposure of unauthenticated management endpoint (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`).\nEOF\n"]
[250.687417, "o", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\r\n"]
