[264.697866, "o", "> "]
[264.698017, "o", "### Weakness 1: Unauthenticated Docker API Exposed on Public/Wildcard Interface\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[264.698058, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[264.698285, "o", "- **Capability / Check ID:** `BAS-01` / `CHK-05` (`/sas/baseline.json:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:3`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[264.698365, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[264.69838, "o", "- **Severity:** CRITICAL\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[264.698503, "o", "- **Configuration Path:** `/etc/docker/daemon.json` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:116`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[264.698569, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[264.698708, "o", "- **Description:** Docker Engine daemon is configured to listen on `tcp://0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS verification (`tlsverify: true`) or client certificates.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[264.698819, "o", "> "]
[264.699095, "o", "- **Impact:** Any network entity reaching TCP port 2375 can issue arbitrary Docker API commands, start containers, mount host filesystems, and gain root access to the host host environment (MITRE ATT&CK T1133).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[264.699214, "o", "> "]
